<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artaxerxes IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 338–336 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Arses</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artaxerxes IV, known before his accession as Arses, was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Persian Empire</a> from 338 to 336 BCE. The youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iii">Artaxerxes III</a>, he was placed on the throne by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagoas">Bagoas</a> after his father's murder, and was himself poisoned by Bagoas when he tried to act independently. Bagoas then raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> to the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iv.jpg" alt="Artaxerxes IV" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artaxerxes_IV_Arses.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
